{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>If a man</b> — Behold, you would command the prophets of HaShem not to preach rebuke against you, so that perhaps you may return to HaShem and not be driven from your land as you drive out those women. Now, if a man comes who prophesies words of falsehood and says to you: Drink and rejoice — HaShem says: For you shall rest in your place, and those who wandered and tottered shall return to their place, as is written after it, I will surely gather and you shall all be assembled. Then will this people's preacher be for you, saying thus — this verse."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:45.764468071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}